# KOVA — Campaign Guides & Email Content

## Campaign Guide Files

Location: src/data/campaigns/
5 files: educational.md, community-branded.md, sales.md, social-proof.md, product-highlights.md

These are Kova's core prompt engineering IP. Do NOT write thin stubs.
Each guide must specify at ~50 lines: section sequence, typography values,
color usage patterns, spacing values, visual hierarchy rules, and anti-patterns.

### Campaign Types:
1. **Educational** — Informative, value-driven. Tips, how-tos, guides.
2. **Community / Branded** — Brand storytelling, welcome sequences, loyalty.
3. **Sales** — Promotions, flash sales, discounts, urgency-driven.
4. **Social Proof** — Reviews, testimonials, user-generated content.
5. **Product Highlights** — New arrivals, launches, collections, showcases.

### Template structure for each guide:
```
# [Type] Email Design Guide

**Campaign intent:** [1-2 sentences]
**Tone:** [descriptive phrase]

**Recommended section sequence (N sections):**
1. Hero — [description with size/weight/bg guidance]
2. Content Block A — [structure + typography details]
3. Content Block B — [variation from A]
4. [Type-specific section] — [unique to this campaign type]
5. CTA + Footer — [CTA style + footer standard]

**Typography rules:**
- Headline: [size]px, [weight], [font], line-height [value]
- Subheadings: [size]px, [weight], line-height [value]
- Body: [size]px, regular, line-height [value]
- Caption: [size]px, muted color

**Color usage:** [specific patterns for this type]
**Spacing & layout:** [padding, gap, corner radius values]
**Visual hierarchy rules:** [2-3 rules]
**Anti-patterns to avoid:** [3-4 things NOT to do]
```

## Email Design Guidelines (always present in system prompt)

Key rules:
- All emails exactly 600px wide (root frame w={600}).
- Emails = stacked sections. Each section: Frame w={600} flex="col".
- Use auto-layout (flex) throughout. No absolute x/y for email content.
  Exception: absolute positioning for decorative overlays/badges WITHIN a section.
- Typography: Headline 32-48px bold, Subheadline 20-24px medium, Body 14-16px regular, Caption 11-12px.
- Line height: 1.4-1.6 body, 1.1-1.2 headlines.
- Section padding: 32-48px vertical, 24-40px horizontal.
- CTA buttons: 16px rounded min, 16/32px padding, contrasting color.
- Dark sections: always set text color explicitly to white/light. Default is BLACK.
- After dark-background render, explicitly verify all child text nodes have light color.
- Use `exportImage` for final visual verification.

## Email JSX Patterns (few-shot examples always in system prompt)

Patterns to include: Hero (dark bg), CTA Section, Two-Column Features, Footer.
Each pattern uses the render tool's JSX syntax with Frame, Text, Rectangle,
Ellipse tags and layout props (flex, gap, items, justify, p/px/py).

## Image Handling Instructions (always in system prompt)

Default: colored rectangle placeholders with descriptive name props.
If user uploaded images before generation: check for existing image nodes
via findNodes/getPageTree and incorporate them.

## Brand Kit Injection Format

```
# Brand: [Client Name]
Primary color: [hex] (use for CTAs, accents, headlines)
Secondary color: [hex] (use for dark sections, footer)
Background: [hex]
Accent: [hex]
Heading font: [font name]
Body font: [font name]
Logo: [node ID if uploaded] OR [not uploaded — use text-based brand name]

Apply these brand values to all design decisions.
```
